  "historical_output_text": " I still remember walking the same trail to and fro, with its winding curves around a lake, through trees of different hues and sizes—this routine path of my life. Each time the leaves turned from the vibrant emulsion of spring's green and pink hues back towards the crisp and cold colors of a fall afternoon; it felt familiar but always with the anticipation that the same old place could be filled by the same or an altered view each passing season brought with its new changes, however slight. \n\nToday's walk had started with a crisp, clear, crisp air. I took my first strides and my mind wandered through familiar trails, each one a familiar friend with a familiar purpose, each step a part and a step closer towards an eventual and inevitable goal—home and the safety that came in that warm and comforting space at its door—until the sound stopped",
